---
export const prerender = true;
import Layout from '../components/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About Chekpoint.gg" variant="centered">
  <div class="about-page">
    <div class="about-header">
      <a href="/" class="back-link">← Chekpoint</a>
      <h1>About Chekpoint.gg</h1>
    </div>

    <div class="about-body">
      <section>
        <h2>What is Chekpoint.gg?</h2>
        <p>Chekpoint.gg is a community-driven platform for video game reviews and discussions. It allows users to share their opinions, follow and create groups with other reviewers, and discover new games.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Why Chekpoint.gg?</h2>
        <p>We wanted a fun name that was video game related and easy to remember. Other fun alternatives we considered were SaveState and GameCabinet among others, we felt that chekpoint was the best fit for us.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Do I need to create an account?</h2>
        <p>You can browse reviews and game pages without an account, but you need to create one to post reviews, follow other users, and participate in groups. Creating an account is free and only requires a valid email address.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Does it cost anything?</h2>
        <p>Using Chekpoint.gg is completely free. We do not charge any fees for browsing reviews, creating accounts, or participating in the community.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>How do I close my account?</h2>
        <p>You may delete your account at any time by navigating to your account settings and selecting "Delete Account." Please note that this action is irreversible and will result in the permanent deletion of your data.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>How should I use Chekpoint?</h2>
        <p>The short answer is however you want to! Our goal is to provide the foundations for community-driven reviews, grouping, tracking and comparing your scores and reviews to others'. A good place to start is the explore page. Here you can discover new games, read reviews and find other user profiles or groups.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What's the difference between marking a game as completed or writing a review?</h2>
        <p>We do not see completing a game as a binary concept. Instead, we encourage users to provide detailed reviews that capture their experience and opinion about a game, regardless of whether they have completed it. Some users may have hundreds of hours invested into a game that has no real end. We feel that everyone with some experience should be able to share their thoughts and opinions about a game.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Can I track a game and review it later?</h2>
        <p>Yes, you can track games on your profile and write reviews at a later time. This allows you to keep a record of your gaming experiences and share your thoughts with the community.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about-page {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 680px;
  }

  .about-header {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    transition: color 0.15s;
  }
  .back-link:hover { color: var(--text-primary); }

  h1 {
    font-family: 'DM Serif Display', serif;
    font-size: 32px;
    font-weight: 400;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .about-body {
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 36px 40px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 28px;
  }

  section { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; }

  h2 {
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
  }

  p, li {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
  }

  a { color: var(--accent); }
  a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .about-body { padding: 24px 20px; }
    h1 { font-size: 26px; }
  }
</style>
